node_modules/
# fork: `dist/` is tracked on purpose. `pi install git:...` clones this repo and
# runs `npm install --omit=dev` (no dev tooling, so nothing can build here), and
# `pi update --extensions` runs `git clean -fdx` before reinstalling, which would
# delete an untracked build. The built bundle therefore ships in the repo, the
# same way the upstream npm tarball does. Rebuild and commit it after every
# source change: `npm run build && git add dist`.coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.tgz
*.log
